│ 2. Process the input data to identify pairs.                                 │
│ 3. Calculate the difference between each pair.                               │
│ 4. Return the maximum difference found.                                      │
│                                                                              │
│ Here's a step-by-step implementation of the `max_difference` function:       │
│                                                                              │
│ ```python                                                                    │
│ def max_difference():                                                        │
│     # Read the input data                                                    │
│     input_data = input().split()                                             │
│     numbers =                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│     # Process the input data to identify pairs                               │
│     pairs = []                                                               │
│     for i in range(len(numbers)):                                            │
│         for j in range(i + 1, len(numbers)):                                 │
│             pairs.append((numbers, numbers))                                 │
│                                                                              │
│     # Calculate the difference between each pair                             │
│     differences = [abs(pair[0] - pair[1]) for pair in pairs]                 │
│                                                                              │
│     # Return the maximum difference found                                    │
│     return max(differences)                                                  │
